  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000, acc≈0.485), the largest source of uncertainty is whether image features carry any useful signal for this task. Testing image_only with a standard resnet50 encoder and singleprofile (config_010) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to the RNA baseline: it isolates the modality question without confounding by aggregation, fusion, or encoder complexity. If image_only performs comparably or better, it justifies investing subsequent budget in multimodal fusion strategies; if it performs poorly, it redirects effort toward improving RNA representations (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. This is the highest-information experiment under the current sparse evidence because it resolves the most fundamental design decision before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

